abraflexi-clientzone (2.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Product detail page (product.php?kod=CODE): description, price with and
    without VAT, unit, type, and above all how the product is paid for - a
    one-time purchase, or a regularly invoiced service (invoiced again every
    month/year until the contract ends) - and what happens after the order.
    Only products the shop sells (labels ESHOP and AKTIVNI) can be shown.
  * The catalog cards show the same badge and link to the detail; search
    results link to it too.
  * How a product is paid for is decided by the label RECURRING or ONETIME of
    the pricelist item, else by the order plugin, else by the unit (a month or
    a year means regular invoicing) and the stock type. A service in hours or
    gigabytes is only "service": nothing more is promised.
  * The price with VAT is counted from the VAT rate of the item (AbraFlexi may
    deliver it equal to the price without VAT for an item entered without VAT).

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:03:05 +0100

abraflexi-clientzone (2.8.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Search works again: it called getColumnsFromFlexibee(), a method the
    current php-abraflexi no longer has, and ended with a fatal error. It now
    looks in the catalog (items labelled ESHOP and AKTIVNI) and, for a signed in
    customer, in the invoices and orders of the customer's company only.
  * The search term is reduced to harmless characters before it enters the
    AbraFlexi filter (a quote in it used to change the filter).

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:33:44 +0100

abraflexi-clientzone (2.8.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * E-mail confirmation no longer finishes the registration when the link is
    merely opened: mail scanners (e.g. Microsoft Safe Links) open every link,
    used up the confirmation and the customer then saw "Registration failed".
    Opening the link shows a button, the customer's own confirmation (POST)
    finishes it. A link used twice for an account that already exists leads
    to the sign in instead of an error.
  * Registration, new customer notice and password mails: Ease\Mailer has
    addText(), not addItem().

